'''''Torenia fournieri''''', the '''bluewings'''<ref>{{PLANTS|id=TOFO2|taxon=Torenia fournieri|accessdate=11 December 2015}}</ref> or '''wishbone flower''', is an annual plant in the [[Linderniaceae]], with blue, white, or pink flowers that have yellow markings. It is typically grown as a landscape annual, reaching 12–15 in. tall. It has simple opposite or subopposite leaves with serrated edges.<ref>{{cite web|last=Gilman|first=Edward F.|author2=Teresa Howe |title=Torenia fournieri|publisher=University of Florida|year=1999|url=http://hort.ifas.ufl.edu/database/documents/pdf/shrub_fact_sheets/torfoua.pdf}}</ref>

